# Check hashes
verify.changed.one=changed file
verify.changed.many=changed files
verify.missing.one=missing file
verify.missing.many=missing files
verify.extra.one=extra file the manifest does not list
verify.extra.many=extra files the manifest does not list
verify.cannot=Cannot check the hashes of “%ls” again: %ls.
verify.empty=“%ls” has no disks read yet: there is nothing to check.
verify.ok.open=“%ls”: %d files checked, all identical to right after the read.
verify.ok.closed=“%ls”: %d files checked, all identical to when the package was closed.
verify.bad=In “%ls” there are %ls (the first: %ls).\n\n%ls
verify.bad.open=Resume the box: when it closes, the disk with the different hash is set aside and asked for again.
verify.bad.closed=The package is no longer intact: put those files back from a copy of the archive, or read the disks again in a new box.
verify.extra.only=Remove the extra files from data: the rest of the package is intact.

